Subject: [PATCH] R81-3 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M48; register rows
 P-810 and P-881; Review 81's item, carried from R80-13 and R79-13): THE
 VERDICT FILES' SCHEMA TEST IS A GATE

P-810: the full suite of Review 79 found eleven verdict files landed in one window that break the schema; the schema's
test refused them, but it was not a gate, and a landing ran only the locks it touched. Main has since run it by hand at
every landing that adds or changes a verdict file.

THE GATE verdict-schema (scripts/gates/gates.py): it loads tests/test_arc_verdict_schema.py and runs its own checks,
test_schema on every verdict file, the census floor, and the kill graph's scope tags; so the rule stands in one place and
the gate cannot drift from the test. A test that cannot be loaded fails the gate (fail-closed); unreadable JSON is a
failure. On the record: every verdict file passes (1,715 of the test's cases).

ITS FAILING PATHS, tests/test_verdict_schema_gate.py, registered in tests/GATE_CONTROLS.json: a verdict file whose scope
carries a key the schema does not have, as P-810's eleven did, fails, and its twin passes (the control); one planted
file per rule (instrument missing, a verdict outside the enum, an id that does not match its folder, no scope, a reach
outside the three, creates_law missing, unreadable JSON), each refused; the gate is registered and passes on the record.

THE RECORD: the register of practices has the gate's section; the changelog and the progress log their entries. No test
of main's is changed. BEFORE: on the tree before this patch the new tests fail.

